# A routine's definition

A routine's `spec` is one JSON object. Every key is spelled exactly as below, and one marked `?` may be left out, to take its default. A key the format doesn't have, or one spelled in another case, is refused. Each part has a topic of its own: `watch`, `triggers` and `schedule`, `conditions` and `fields`, `steps`, `agent`, `github`, and `limits`.

```
Spec {
  version: 1
  watch: Watch
  trigger: Trigger
  conditions: Conditions
  steps: Step[]
  limits: Limits
  notify?: Notices
  requires?: string[]
}
Watch {
  sources: Source[]
}
Trigger {
  event: string  // a trigger's event: topic triggers
  waitForChecks?: boolean
  settleMinutes?: number
  firstToo?: boolean
  ownPushesToo?: boolean
  count?: number
  days?: number
  label?: string
  schedule?: Schedule
}
Conditions {
  match: "all" | "any"
  of: Clause[]
}
Step {  // exactly one kind of step, and onlyIf
  notify?: NotifyStep
  pin?: Empty
  snooze?: SnoozeStep
  dismiss?: Empty
  restore?: Empty
  markDone?: Empty
  github?: GitHubAction[]
  agent?: AgentStep
  waitForChecks?: WaitStep
  merge?: MergeStep
  postReview?: ReviewStep
  tellMe?: TellStep
  script?: ScriptStep
  onlyIf?: "passed" | "stillFails" | "pushed" | "notPushed" | "approve" | "requestChanges"
}
Limits {
  oncePer?: "item" | "headCommit" | "day"
  triesPerItem?: number
  runsPerDay?: number
  waitMinutes?: number
  activeHours?: ActiveHours
  budgetPerDay?: Budget
}
Notices {
  alert?: boolean
  needsYou?: boolean
  finished?: boolean
  checks?: boolean
  problem?: boolean
}
Source {  // exactly one of lists and search
  lists?: ("reviewRequested" | "authored" | "assigned")[]
  search?: Search
}
Schedule {
  every: "day" | "weekday" | "week"
  at: string
  on?: "mon" | "tue" | "wed" | "thu" | "fri" | "sat" | "sun"
  style?: "each" | "digest"
}
Clause {  // a condition (field, op, and value or values), or a group
  field?: string  // a field's id: topic fields
  op?: string  // an operator: topic conditions
  value?: string
  values?: string[]
  group?: Conditions
}
NotifyStep {
  note?: string
  banner?: boolean
}
Empty {  // no keys: {}
}
SnoozeStep {
  days?: number
}
GitHubAction {  // exactly one action
  rebase?: Empty
  updateBranch?: Empty
  reply?: ReplyAction
  labels?: LabelsAction
}
AgentStep {
  agent?: string
  prompt: PromptRef
  where?: "background" | "terminal"
  profile?: string
  fallbacks?: ProfileRef[]
  model?: string
  effort?: string
  planMode?: boolean
  worktree?: boolean
  launchFor?: LaunchRow[]
  fence?: Fence
}
WaitStep {
  settleMinutes?: number
  giveUpHours?: number
}
MergeStep {
  how: "autoMergeIfItWasOn" | "whenMergeable"
  method?: "merge" | "squash" | "rebase"
  allowBypass?: boolean
  allowSensitive?: boolean
}
ReviewStep {
  as: "comment" | "verdict"
  allowApprove?: boolean
}
TellStep {
  when?: "reached" | "verdict"
}
ScriptStep {
  id: number
  name: string
}
ActiveHours {
  days: ("mon" | "tue" | "wed" | "thu" | "fri" | "sat" | "sun")[]
  from: string
  to: string
}
Budget {  // exactly one of usd and tokens
  usd?: number
  tokens?: number
}
Search {
  kind?: "pr" | "issue"
  authors?: string[]
  where?: string[]
  involving?: ("assigned" | "reviewRequested" | "mentioned")[]
  labels?: string[]
  notLabels?: string[]
  base?: string
  headPrefix?: string
  state?: ("ready" | "draft" | "failing" | "passing" | "pending" | "changesRequested" | "approved" | "reviewRequired" | "unreviewed")[]
  more?: string
}
ReplyAction {
  prompt: PromptRef
}
LabelsAction {
  add?: string[]
  remove?: string[]
}
PromptRef {  // exactly one of starter, nickname, and itemDefault
  starter?: string
  nickname?: string
  itemDefault?: boolean
}
ProfileRef {
  agent: string
  profile: string
}
LaunchRow {
  target: string
  agent?: string
  profile?: string
  model?: string
  effort?: string
}
Fence {
  budget?: Budget
  timeoutMinutes?: number
  tools?: "readOnly" | "githubTasks" | "editTest" | "editTestPush" | "profile"
  allow?: string[]
  deny?: string[]
}
```

- `version` is always 1, the format this build reads and writes.
- `notify` says which of the routine's notices show a banner (`true`) or only an entry in the Notifications page (`false`); a key left out follows Settings → Notifications. `alert` is its Notify me and Tell me, `needsYou` a match that waits for the user's OK, `finished` its agent's run ending, `checks` Wait for the checks' verdict, and `problem` the routine failing to run.
- `requires` names the programs the routine needs beyond what Nilbox works out on its own, such as `pnpm` or `govulncheck`, at most 20.
- A routine's name and description sit beside its definition, in the proposal's routine; its mode and its switch are the user's.
